<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Muthul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">109 BCE</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Muthul was fought in 109 BCE near the Muthul River in Numidia between the Roman army of the consul Quintus Caecilius Metellus and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>. Jugurtha ambushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> on the march, but after a hard day's fighting Metellus drove off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numidians">Numidians</a>. The battle did not end the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a>, as Jugurtha turned to raids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare.</p></div>
